From 2eca6b7412041d01ad8690d80fec15f87bd39a4c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cizar-szymon <szymon@cs-lab.eu>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 17:21:49 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 05/11] Faster loading and saving of text saves

The map sections looked their values up for every tile (a name copied,
lowered and searched in a map, ten times per tile), the lists were split
with a stringstream, every number was parsed with 64-bit strtoull and
written with its own ostringstream. On a 68060 (Warp) a save of 126 KB
took 2.2 s to load and 3.4 s to save.

Now the values are looked up once per section, lists are split with
find(), parts built in place, numbers parsed and written in 32 bits.
The output is byte for byte the same (CRC of a load-and-save round
trip unchanged): saving 3.4 -> 0.5 s, loading 2.2 -> 1.0 s (0.57 s with
the Amiga port's size-class allocator).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Uqv2KDnCV91tQsZeLq3naz
